WEBVTT

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.040
The ocean!

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.790
Hot ramen!

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:08.640
We roared about and had fun, but in the end,

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:13.440
we get stuck with unreasonable operations the military thinks up.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.680
We're supposed to be all stressed out, but

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.150
I don't know if everyone is resilient or just thickheaded.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.690
The Kursk Industrial Region...

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.840
Long before we were born, it prospered as a military complex

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.510
specializing in the development of land based weapons systems.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:11.110
Now Kursk is occupied by the Jovian Lizards.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.190
And to make it worse,

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.320
those bastards have deployed a new weapons platform that's never been encountered anywhere else!

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:22.200
So, our mission is the destruction of this new enemy weapon, right?

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:24.230
That's correct.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.120
Headquarters' code name for it is "The Walkingstick."

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:26.800
Finding Yourself in a "Routine Plot"?

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.850
Special demolitions teams have been sent after it three times,

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:31.540
but no one has returned alive yet.
Finding Yourself in a "Routine Plot"?

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.450
How uneconomical.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.420
That's where the Nadesico comes in!

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.900
The Gravity Blast Cannon will take care of it!

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.950
I see. A long range strike.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:41.720
Exactly!

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.760
I suppose that's the safest.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.140
I agree from an economical standpoint.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.120
This way the Aestivalis won't be vulnerable to attack either.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.310
Oh, don't beat around the bush like that, Megu-chan.

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:54.150
You mean, " Akito-san won't be vulnerable."

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:56.220
I suppose so.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:57.940
My, my! Aren't we forthright?

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.190
We'll start the operation immediately!

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:00.720
Tenkawa Akito

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.500
If only you were more reliable,

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:02.650
Tenkawa Akito

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.030
that mechanical monster wouldn't have gotten away!

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.200
I'm tired of listening to you whine and gripe!

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.120
You bastard!

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.090
Stop fighting, Ken! Quit it now, Joe!

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.300
Fighting won't do anything! You have to stop!

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.450
Teammates?

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:17.560
Fighting won't do anything! You have to stop!

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:20.770
Eight minutes, thirty seconds until operation commencement.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.290
Connecting energy bypass feed to Gravity Blast Cannon.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:26.220
As soon as the Gravity Blast is charged,

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.670
clear the mountain to fire!

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:30.100
Make this one really count!

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:32.770
17000 to designated operation point.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.860
Your punch leaves a mark.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.010
So does yours!

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:42.950
You've made up!

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:43.280
Hand shaking is the best way to make up! Shake those hands!

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.870
But a fight rarely ends like that in real life.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:49.290
Phase Transition Engine, all systems condition green.

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:52.910
Distortion Field Strength, down thirteen percent.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.290
Final safety mechanism unlocked.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.610
1500 to designated operation point.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:02.470
800 to designated operation point.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.600
Incoming enemy round.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.230
Did something hit us?!

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.440
We've lost the Distortion Field!

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:21.850
Over eighteen blocks were damaged by that hit.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.530
The Phase Transition Engine has shut down!

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.500
The Walkingstick must be a gravity wave rail gun.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:28.460
Losing control! We're about to crash!

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:30.320
They create an incredibly controlled micro black hole,

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:31.320
Giving full power to auxiliary engine.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.630
accelerate it and fire it as a projectile!

00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:35.210
Thanks, but we have more pressing affairs at hand!

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:47.510
While powerful, it takes time to make another micro black hole.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.150
So I think we will be safe for a while.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.930
Thank you for such a reassuring opinion.

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.260
But what should we do now?

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.060
I suppose it's the Aestivalis' turn.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:59.250
Anti-air defense system...

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.430
All previous infiltration attempts were annihilated by this.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:05.740
They will be able to hit us even at this location.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:08.960
Please inform us of such important things sooner!

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.800
Oh? I didn't mention it?

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.660
Then the Aestivalis won't fair any better if they approach by air.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:18.120
I'm getting a headache thinking about the economic inefficiencies.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:20.350
The pilots would be suffering something far worse than that.

00:05:20.780 --> 00:05:21.560
Absolutely.

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:24.190
Approach from the sky is out.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:27.850
To create a micro black hole, the Walkingstick needs twelve hours.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:30.930
We were hit at 1700, so the next one will come at 0500 tomorrow.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:30.990
Yes, thank you for such a valuable opinion!

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:32.340
We have little time.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:33.510
A team must be sent in, or we'll be in trouble.

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:33.520
Yes, thank you for such a valuable opinion!

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:34.280
Yes, yes. We understand. Thanks for everything.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.860
Then I suppose we'll have to approach on land.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:35.930
Yes, yes. We understand. Thanks for everything.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:37.390
And so...

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:39.910
Aestivalis will approach by land, and destroy the Walkingstick.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:41.360
Operations will commence in one hour.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:42.130
18:00
Pilot Briefing

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:46.510
We'll have two in configuration 04, and three in configuration 01.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:46.520
18:00
Pilot Briefing

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.550
Akatsuki will be tactical C&C!

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:49.000
Yes, Sir!

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.640
You'll be in charge.

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:51.950
I'll do my best, everyone!

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:56.570
You'll be operating a considerable distances away from the Nadesico, so you won't be able to recharge.

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:57.370
That's why...

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:59.330
Take this external battery!

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.250
Attach it to each land combat configured Aestivalis!

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:04.150
Got that?!

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:08.550
Akatsuki-san, I sure hope we'll succeed with this mission.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:11.760
I'm sure we'll pull it off as long as we work together!

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:12.610
Yes! A lucky hit!
OF COURSE we will...

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:14.870
OF COURSE we will...

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:18.310
Thank you. Thank God, I was running low on credits.
An able commander is the base of a successful operation!

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.410
Would you like some juice too, Akito-kun?

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:20.570
How about a Mars Soda?
An able commander is the base of a successful operation!

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:22.480
It takes more than that!
How about a Mars Soda?

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:23.650
You're right!

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.570
The commander doesn't fight a war.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:30.540
Careful preparations up front are important, like rigorous training.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:33.190
No, that's not what I mean.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.330
Here! Your juice, Akito-kun!

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.540
It takes teamwork.

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:46.960
What's up?

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.500
Did I say something inappropriate?

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:54.930
Then or dear old teammate Tenkawa Akito-kun
can be our quartermaster!

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.470
Perfect!

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.040
He's a real team member after all.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.140
What is that suppose to mean?

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:02.330
Exactly that.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:03.190
Baka.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.360
Akito is the quartermaster!

00:07:05.990 --> 00:07:07.820
Pile it all, all of it, on him!

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:08.780
Gotcha!

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:13.180
Well, I guess we hardly have any teammates around here.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.320
Fifteen minutes to operations commencement.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:18.830
All pilots and mechanics, please conduct final check procedures.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:19.910
Yeah, sure.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:20.640
Akito-san...

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:25.220
Don't worry. This is a private line. No one can hear us.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:28.560
Do you mind?

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:29.240
I understand that your opponent this time is this hideous weapon.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:32.330
Hey, Akito? How's the camera eye's vision?

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:32.700
So I... I'm so worried.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:33.400
Hey, Akito? How's the camera eye's vision?

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.130
Okay! It's fine.
So I... I'm so worried.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:36.010
Please make it back safely!

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.740
All clear for Akito's Aestivalis!

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.840
I know you might make fun of me for saying this,

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:45.270
but if you can make it back safely,

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:48.420
I'm sure that our relationship will advance a lot farther!

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:51.280
Just a second. I have an incoming priority message.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:52.530
Akito...

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:54.190
Yurika!

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:57.950
Don't worry. This is a private line so no one else can listen in.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:07:59.460
Do you have a moment?

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:01.950
I understand that your opponent this time is this hideous weapon.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:04.110
Tenkawa! Akito!

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:04.270
I understand that your opponent this time is this hideous weapon.

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:05.040
Hey! Hello?!

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.790
So I... I'm so worried.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:07.430
Damn.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:08.150
Please make it back safely.
Does anyone here know how to send priority messages?

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.100
Does anyone here know how to send priority messages?
Please make it back safely.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.190
Does anyone here know how to send priority messages?

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.570
I know you might make fun of me for saying this,

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:18.170
but if you can make it back safely, I'm sure that our relationship...

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.150
...will advance a lot, right?

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:24.670
I'm so happy! You feel the same way about this, Akito!

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.940
Well, that's not what I...

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:28.350
Just hold on a second!

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.790
Oh man, what should I do?

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:36.760
Tenkawa!

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:38.930
I'm sorry, I was wrong!

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:41.230
I'll be a good person from now on! Really! Please forgive me!

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:42.760
What the hell are you talking about?

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.980
Howmei-san's been screaming at you for a while.

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:47.400
Didn't you notice?

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:49.590
There you are.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:50.040
Baka.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:54.700
I figured simple rations are too dry and bland,
so I loaded up your Aestivalis with lots of food!

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:57.400
But this is way more than we'll ever need!

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:02.150
A first class chef has to be able to prepare any dish he's asked for!

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.850
Akito-kun, we're teammates, right?

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.540
We're counting on you, Tenkawa.

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.640
Just remember all the broads that have their hearts set on you.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:10.690
Oh God...

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:11.980
You never had it any better than this!

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:16.250
Oh, I envy you so much, Tenkawa Akito!

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:19.920
We're green with envy, Tenkawa Akito!

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.160
BAKA-bakka, everyone Baka.

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:24.230
Salute!

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:25.590
My...

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:28.380
A new Cosplay?

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:30.830
Seiya-san said if we wore these...

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:34.460
We'd feel more like we're working at an operations headquarters.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:37.300
So he got these out of his collection.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:38.390
Salute!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:41.430
How do I look?

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:42.740
My...

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:44.560
We've started working on our end as well.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:49.020
The Doctor is analyzing the latest data from the spy satellites.

00:09:51.030 --> 00:09:53.110
Soon we should have more information to work with.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:57.450
Aestivalis units are now beyond reach of our energy feed system.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:58.240
Salute!

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.660
Really, BAKA-bakka.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:05.200
Well, perhaps you don't like doing this?

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.460
I'm not a child.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:18.570
Hey, is dinner almost ready?

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:20.280
Yes, yes!

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.700
Oh, I just love how woks can pass through the heat so well!

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:25.260
Baka?

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:35.090
All right! We'll take off in forty-five minutes!

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.480
Use this time to get some shut...

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:39.760
Oh wow, lzumi's way ahead of us.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.090
Right! I'll be sleeping for a while now as well.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:44.840
Oh sure, go ahead.

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:45.510
All right!

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:51.260
Looks like they're enjoying their youth.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:55.750
Our dreams call out for tomorrow

00:11:55.750 --> 00:12:00.910
Listen to our soul yell out, Let's go, passion...

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:01.570
Ahem!

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:05.400
What's up, Ryoko..-san?

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.440
Hey, Tenkawa, you're a real dope, aren't you?

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:10.560
What's all this all of a sudden?

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.030
Here! Eat up!

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:14.050
Thanks.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.750
You were so busy, you didn't get a chance to eat much, did you?

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:17.830
Eat up!

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:22.360
Just watching you gets on my nerves, you know that?

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:27.540
Whatever! Just don't worry about it. All right?!

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:30.000
Anyway, just eat up!

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:33.430
Hey, this tastes pretty good!

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:36.160
Baka. You're the one who made it.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.190
Oh, that's right.

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:38.880
Baka!

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:40.250
Hey, you two!

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.510
You seem to be living in a coming of age movie, but I have to say,

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:45.660
this is a little unhealthy for my tastes.

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:49.470
I don't think it's a good idea to let yourself be influenced by him, Ryoko-kun.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.330
What is that supposed to mean?

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.790
You know, people like you who like anime and stuff

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:55.260
like to disguise their shortcomings in relationships

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:57.250
by saying that they're only interested in platonic love.

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:01.630
It would be unfortunate if you fell into a trap like that.

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.670
You have to be more open and outgoing!

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:06.500
Oh, excuse me.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:08.600
I shouldn't imply that you're not good at romantic relationships.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:13.320
The Captain and Megu-chan certainly are hot and bothered over you.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:14.200
Let me correct myself.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:15.190
That's not the point!

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:17.530
I don't like it when people put down other people's hobbies!

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:20.360
Well in that case, I'll have to correct my correction.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.280
I don't like anime and stuff.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:24.030
What did I ever do to you?

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:25.950
My line exactly.

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:31.230
What's up?

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:33.060
Guess we're under fire.

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:43.010
Under attack?

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:45.750
Yes! We'll relay you the visual.

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:50.850
Drinking too much... Getting tanked...

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:52.280
Tanks?

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:54.210
Well, it's no surprise you're not familiar with them.

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:57.370
The primary land combat weapon two generations ago were tanks.

00:13:57.370 --> 00:13:59.350
That's right! The proper jargon for it is A.F. V!

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:00.670
I see. Using tanks to protect the land approach is quite clever.

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:03.480
Or in other words, Armored Fighting Vehicle.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:03.740
Put even cooler, it's "Sonderkraftfahrzeug"!

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:05.800
Improvisation with locally available sources.

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:05.830
Put even cooler, it's "Sonderkraftfahrzeug"!

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:07.490
They're pretty economical at allocating their resources.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:08.500
Enough, you military-tech geek!

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.070
We should take heed of this as well.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:13.670
Akito and Akatsuki, go on ahead!

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:14.230
Thank you!

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:15.460
I'll stay and fight!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:20.320
While it may be outdated, there is threat in numbers.

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:22.320
Captain, we have trouble.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:22.790
Yes?

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:25.440
I don't have all the data, but it's bad news.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:26.460
How bad?

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:28.190
Well, quite bad.

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:29.550
Damn!

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:30.980
Enough!

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:31.770
Why'd you do that?!

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:33.250
Stop wasting ammunition!

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:37.000
This heavy artillery frame is all we have against the Walkingstick!

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:38.770
Let Ryoko and the others take care of this.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:40.100
So, we just watch while they get pummeled?!

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:43.540
Damn!

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:46.990
The batteries...

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:48.590
Now look at what we're stuck with!

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:49.320
Shut the hell up!

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:50.820
Stop this!

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:51.920
Shove it!

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:52.550
Stop, Tenkawa Akito! Cool your head!

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:54.950
Damn! Damn! Damn!

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.460
Now, are we feeling satisfied?

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:08.730
I have some bad news.

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:09.970
The Walkingstick is coming alive.

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:15.150
I don't have enough data to tell just how soon until it fires again,

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:18.750
but I can say that damage from the next blast will be far worse.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:19.850
What do you mean?

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:24.820
The first micro black hole broke up outside the atmosphere,

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:25.770
resulting in little residual damage.

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:29.690
I'm sure the next one will break up within the atmosphere.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:31.930
Why are you so sure about that?

00:15:32.390 --> 00:15:33.620
Because I don't believe our enemies are fools.

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:36.530
And so, this is what will end up happening.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:40.450
The tremendous radiation will instantly boil away the city.

00:15:40.770 --> 00:15:43.390
Anything that survives will suffer massive gamma ray exposure.

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:45.890
Modify operation pattern from A to D.

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:46.460
Roger!

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:48.880
Have a good time!

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:50.910
Come back, all right?!

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:51.800
You just do that!

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:54.050
They'd better make it back.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:58.230
Or else we'd be in a real pinch. We're immobilized now.

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:01.940
Yeah, you're right. We gave them all the remaining batteries.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.140
Oh, this bites.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.360
We're running low on both energy and ammunition.

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:15.110
Make sure to keep your grand standing to a minimum.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:15.810
Got that?

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:16.880
Roger.

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.110
Who do you think you are?

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:24.200
What the hell?!

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:27.250
This one looks a little more menacing than the previous toys.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.130
Jeez!

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:35.070
The Aestivalis are fitted with suction mines! Use them!

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:37.210
Yeah, all right! We're on it.

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:42.250
This is hopeless.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:44.510
Hikaru, how about that mine?!

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:45.850
Just wait a second!

00:16:49.890 --> 00:16:51.490
All right, I got it!

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.190
Oh no!

00:16:57.790 --> 00:16:57.890
Oh, my poor Aesti-chan!

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:01.780
The armor on the bottom is always the thinnest for tanks!

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:02.410
I got it!

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:05.350
That's why you should go after the bottom, or the hull, of the tanks.

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:07.340
When I'm talking about hulls, I mean the tank and not a ship.

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:08.590
I got it! I got it!

00:17:08.590 --> 00:17:09.220
When I'm talking about hulls, I mean the tank and not a ship.

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:21.750
Perfect kiss... Bulls eye...

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:23.420
Yeah, yeah, whatever.

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:24.820
There you go, my soldiers.

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:28.440
If you hit their weak spot hard, your hands alone can be enough!

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:30.490
Yeah, you're right! Isn't it amazing?

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:32.240
I'm impressed!

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:35.190
Emergency alert. Evacuate now!

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.470
How can we evacuate when our Aesti-chan's are immobile?

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:39.120
Well...

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:42.700
We're running into some serious obstacles here, and...

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.500
Damn!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:47.620
Hold it! Be patient!

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:49.540
Then what the hell are we supposed to do?!

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:05.840
Graviton wave fluctuation increasing. It's coming!

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:07.350
Repairs won't be done in time!

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:10.500
What are we going to do?! What are we going to do?!

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:13.740
What am I going to tell headquarters about this?!

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:14.590
Please keep quiet!

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.390
Thank you for all your cooperation, Admiral.

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:18.860
Salute!

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:23.290
The captain certainly knows how to keep her head when it heats up.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.830
It's because you believe in him, isn't it?

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.610
We'll make a run for the Walkingstick.

00:18:29.150 --> 00:18:30.580
You got that, Tenkawa-kun?

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:32.100
I got it.

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:33.620
I got it, but...

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:37.620
Looks like you two are in a tight spot!

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:38.260
Yahoo!

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:39.830
You're just in time.

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:41.670
Well, we're teammates after all.

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:43.430
Guess we know what's next.

00:18:43.870 --> 00:18:45.190
What's that?

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:47.520
Dear Tenkawa-kun just doesn't get it.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.760
Your job's to go after the Walkingstick!

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:53.150
Our job's to pin down this tank here.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.290
That's the idea!

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:55.360
What's the idea?

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:58.940
You head to the Walkingstick. We go after the tank!

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:00.660
Let's go!

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:02.200
Go!

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:08.940
Everyone, hold tight!

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:09.750
What are you going to do?

00:19:10.220 --> 00:19:11.290
Ram him!

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:14.420
Oh man, with your personality, there's no stopping, is there?!

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:17.000
Now, you long-haired show off!

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:18.010
Got you!

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:21.750
And this is how you knock out a big old tank!

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:24.900
Oh no you don't!

00:19:29.420 --> 00:19:30.180
Yes!

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:34.560
Hurry!

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:35.190
Low Power on
Backup Battery!

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:37.280
Just a little more. Just a little more!

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:39.690
There! Fire all guns!

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:48.030
Warning!
Almost Empty

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:50.660
If I hadn't wasted my ammunition back there...

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:53.300
Oh damn, I knew it!

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:58.250
Now you see why I said don't waste your ammo?

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:04.920
Emergency!
Backup Battery Empty

00:20:04.920 --> 00:20:05.840
Thanks.

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:06.290
Emergency!
Backup Battery Empty

00:20:06.290 --> 00:20:08.260
Great work. Great work.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:08.300
Emergency!
Backup Battery Empty

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:10.740
All in all, you did a great job!

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:12.010
Yahoo!

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:14.050
Akatsuki here. Mission's over.

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.350
It'd be nice if you'd come to pick us up.

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:16.900
Roger.

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:18.970
Everyone!

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:22.860
A lot happened, but...

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:25.620
You did a great job, Tenkawa Akito-kun.

00:20:26.440 --> 00:20:27.330
You outdid yourself.

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:34.870
Oh, there she comes.

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:38.060
I got an idea for my next fan comic!

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:40.000
When friendship between men turns into...

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:48.780
What? You want me to participate in the character popularity poll?

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:50.960
Well, there's Minato-san with adult glamour abloom.

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:52.720
But wait, Hikaru-chan does look good with her glasses.

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:54.700
Then there is the Captain with her breasts.

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:57.000
But I guess "BAKA-bakka", is the best.

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.150
Right! My vote is for Hoshino Ruri!

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:01.790
Next Martian Successor Nadesico: "Those Unforgettable Days"

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:05.380
It's the second installment of the three part Hoshino Ruri saga.

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:07.500
Screenplay again by Takeshi Shishido.

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:08.380
Make sure everyone casts their votes...

00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:11.260
I mean, watch the next episode of Nadesico!
